.TITLE "dmesg"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Displays the system message buffer. It shows messages generated by the __kernel__ and device drivers during system operation and boot.

.DIV "ALIAS"

.DIV "TLDR"
**dmesg**
Displays all messages currently held in the kernel message buffer.
> 

**sudo dmesg**
Runs the command with administrative privileges to ensure all messages are visible.
> 

.DIV "SUMMARY"
On macOS, __dmesg__ is often used to debug hardware connection issues or kernel panics. Because it interacts with system-level logs, it frequently requires __sudo__ for full access to the buffer.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:sudo** **mac:sysctl**

documentation: __https://ss64.com/osx/dmesg.html__
